From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/34] coherent: split plan_left_planned from plan_left; lanes
 for a reader planned in part

r2 counted plan_left 34 (= plan_copies_back): each late batch's copy back
left a record of a command buffer with an unplanned batch. That is exact
where none of it is planned (plan_left). Where it is planned in part, its
planned writes land only at its completion, over the batch's write through
another import unless the reader's work after its wait uses the surface
(path 4 copies it in): counted plan_left_planned. Lane
..._planned_in_part passes; ..._planned_in_part_elsewhere_after shows the
gap and is ignored until records keep their areas by part.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
